# Run locally

The local install keeps everything on one machine: the app, the SQLite database and the API keys. It is the quickest way to try the reader.

## Install

Use the [installer](/docs/install) for your platform, or run it once without installing:

<CopyCommand command="npx last30days-news" />

## Start it

<CopyCommand command="last30days" />

The command starts at `http://127.0.0.1:4477`, opens your browser and prints the data directory. The first run uses the password `last30`. Change it in Settings after you sign in.

Use `--no-open` when you do not want a browser window:

<CopyCommand command="last30days --no-open" />

If port 4477 is busy, the command tries 4477 through 4487. Pin one when you need a stable address:

<CopyCommand command="PORT=4480 last30days" />

On Windows PowerShell:

<CopyCommand command="$env:PORT = 4480; last30days" />

`HOST` defaults to `127.0.0.1`. Keep it there unless a reverse proxy is in front of the app.

## Where the data lives

| Platform | Default data directory |
| --- | --- |
| Windows | `%APPDATA%\last30days-news` |
| macOS | `~/Library/Application Support/last30days-news` |
| Linux | `$XDG_DATA_HOME/last30days-news`, or `~/.local/share/last30days-news` |

Set `L30_DATA_DIR` to use another folder. The database is `<data-dir>/db.sqlite`, with WAL mode and foreign keys enabled.

To back it up, stop the app and copy the whole data directory. Copying only `db.sqlite` while the app is running can miss the WAL file.

## Environment variables

The packaged app reads variables from the shell. It does not load `.env.development` or `.env.production` by itself.

- `PORT` and `HOST` control the listen address.
- `L30_DATA_DIR` moves the SQLite file.
- `L30_DEBUG=1` adds verbose logs.
- `L30_TRUST_PROXY=1` only when a reverse proxy overwrites `X-Forwarded-For` and `X-Forwarded-Proto`.

See [configuration](/docs/configuration) for the full list.

## Reset the local password

Open `http://127.0.0.1:4477/reset` from the same machine. Reset clears the password, saved API keys and sessions. Items, sources and categories stay.

The route is loopback only. A remote client gets `403 reset_local_only`. See [passwords and recovery](/docs/passwords).

## Update

Run the installer again, or update the global package:

<CopyCommand command="npm install --global https://github.com/Emmraan/last30days-news/releases/latest/download/last30days-news.tgz" />

Your database stays in the data directory and is migrated on the next start.

